00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:50.560
we're trying to figure out is what is
your attention span for an individual

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:56.410
subject so if we know that this person
can pay attention to history for one

00:07:56.410 --> 00:08:02.500
hour and after that you know her mind
starts wandering then it's complete

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:07.690
waste of time literally to spend more
than one hour studying history at a time

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:13.600
that's what I call a compartment of time
so if it comes to your writing how much

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:18.490
time can you write being fully focused
and not thinking about the outside world

00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:23.790
etc and that's the compartment that
where your attention span is at its max

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:29.020
because if you're doing anything where
your attention span is not at its max

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:35.169
you are basically wasting your time and
your energy and those both of those

00:08:35.169 --> 00:08:40.560
things have a negative kind of
depressive effect on your motivation

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:45.490
they're not good so you really want to
figure out your attention span and then

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:50.320
you want to arrange your life in
compartments of time that have to do

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:56.170
with attention span
and when it comes to being conscious of

00:08:56.170 --> 00:09:01.810
time one of my rules has been from the
very first time I started thinking of

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:06.310
these things when I was like 19 so I
stopped wearing a watch because I

00:09:06.310 --> 00:09:10.600
realized that the only way I was going
to be productive with my kind of

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:16.180
interests and activities was if I lived
in my own time and did not live in

00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:20.440
everybody else's time but everywhere you
look there's a clock on the wall there's

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:27.490
big big bin on the horizon there's you
know television monitors with countdowns

00:09:27.490 --> 00:09:31.480
on them there's everything out there
reminding you of the world's time and

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:37.060
the world's time is not your time you
don't have all the time in the world you

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:41.680
have your own time so I discovered a
method years ago which is simply the

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:47.050
stopwatch method which is that instead
of using clocks use stopwatch and you

00:09:47.050 --> 00:09:51.730
tell yourself for example I'm going to
write for an hour and a half today no

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:57.160
matter what and I'm going to monitor
that on a stopwatch and I will turn the

00:09:57.160 --> 00:10:01.720
